STEP 9: VERIFY NEW TESTS EXERCISE ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA
=====================================================

Acceptance Criterion AC2: "App tests through the app server client with scripted dropping streams: the 300 s resume allowance applies per outage and resets after every successful resume, so several short outages in one reply all resume; a single outage longer than 300 s ends the reply on the phone with error status and its steps kept."

New test (a) in APIClient per-outage resume allowance describe block:
  "several 200 s outages in one reply all resume, even though the total outage time exceeds 300 s"
  - Creates 4 sequential drops, each lasting 200 s of fake time (total 800 s)
  - Asserts all 5 resume requests are made
  - Asserts onError does not fire, onComplete does fire
  - Asserts all events arrive exactly once in order
  - EXERCISES: Multiple short outages in one reply all resume successfully

New test (b) in APIClient per-outage resume allowance describe block:
  "a single outage longer than 300 s after an earlier short outage ends the reply with an error and no further requests"
  - Creates initial request + stream
  - First outage: 100 s (successful)
  - Second outage: 300+ s (fails with error)
  - Asserts state.completed is false
  - Asserts state.errored is not null (error message contains "connection to the Mac was lost")
  - Asserts only 3 fetch calls made (not 4)
  - EXERCISES: Single outage longer than 300 s ends the reply with error

New test (c) in APIClient per-outage resume allowance describe block:
  "the allowance is measured from the start of the current outage: 299 s still retries, over 300 s does not"
  - First outage: 250 s (successful)
  - Second outage: Tries at 299 s (still within budget, makes request)
  - Second outage: Tries again at 301 s (exceeds budget, fails)
  - Asserts 4 fetch calls made
  - Asserts 3 sleeps happen
  - Asserts final error is thrown
  - EXERCISES: Budget reset per outage, 299s retries but 300+ doesn't

New test in conversationSession describe block:
  "ends the reply with status error and keeps its steps when the connection never comes back within 300 s"
  - Emits 2 step events then drops the connection
  - Simulates connection never coming back (all resume attempts fail)
  - Advances 200+ s of fake time per attempt
  - Asserts reply.status === "error"
  - Asserts reply.steps contains the 2 emitted steps
  - EXERCISES: Outage longer than 300s ends with error and steps are kept

